# ── dependencies and build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── capture harness output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# shots/ is where every tool writes its frames. It is ~2.8 GB and every file in
# it is regenerable with `node tools/shot.mjs`, so it stays out of history.
shots/

# review/ is deliberately TRACKED, not ignored: the archived contact sheets are
# the visual record of the project and the art director judges rounds from them.
# See review/INDEX.md.

# reference-art/ is deliberately TRACKED: it is the art target every visual
# judgement is measured against. Do not add it here, and do not delete from it.

# ── world bakes ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# public/bakes/ is generated, not source. Run `node tools/bake.mjs` once after
# cloning; it writes the .pab bakes and manifest.json in ~25 s per resolution.
#
# These were tracked until 2026-08-21, on the reasoning that a fresh clone
# should run without waiting for a bake. That trade stopped being worth it:
#
#   * Players never received these files anyway. vite.config.js deletes every
#     .pab from dist/ at build time, because Cloudflare rejects any asset over
#     25 MiB and the 1536 bake is 44 MB. Production serves bakes from R2 via
#     VITE_BAKE_BASE_URL, and a client with no bake at all bakes live in a
#     worker (src/main.js — `loadCachedBake() ?? bakeWorld()`). The tracked
#     copies only ever saved *developers* the one-time bake.
#   * They cost 387 MB of the 637 MB .git. Every edit to TerrainGen.js changes
#     the generator hash and produces a whole new 44 MB incompressible blob.
#     tools/bake.mjs prunes stale bakes from disk correctly, but git history
#     keeps every generation forever regardless of the delete.
#
# So: 25 s of CPU once per clone, against a repository nobody could clone.
public/bakes/

# ── local noise ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# ── scratch ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# tools/_scratch/ holds one-off diagnostic instruments and IS tracked — several
# of them (cost2, tierload, wdrive's ancestors) are load-bearing. Only their
# output is ignored.
tools/_scratch/**/out/
tools/_scratch/**/*.png
